# Build output. Every image in here embeds the whole of Combat, so this has to
# stay out for the same reason rom/ does, quite apart from being generated.
build/

# THE CARTRIDGE ITSELF IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# Combat is Atari's, 1977, and the commented disassembly is Harry Dodgson's,
# Nick Bensema's and Roger Williams' work on top of it. This project is a patch
# and a server; it is not a place to redistribute either. Supply your own dump
# and disassembly -- see rom/README.md for the two files and the md5 the build
# checks against.
rom/*.bin
rom/*.asm

# The C relay's binary. server/c/ itself is source and belongs in the tree.
server/c/combat-relay

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors and the usual detritus
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
